+---
+title: Testing click.utils to full coverage
+author: HarzerHeribert
+date: 2026-10-15
+cost: { minutes: 2, tokens: 57065 }
+touches:
+  - tests/test_utils/test_utils_more.py
+  - src/click/utils.py
+---
+
+## Decided
+- Coverage tests for src/click/utils.py live in tests/test_utils/test_utils_more.py; they take utils.py to 100% lines+branches without touching src/.
+- Windows paths of get_app_dir are tested by monkeypatching `click.utils.WIN` (imported at module level from _compat), and sys.platform for darwin/linux.
+- `"-"` stream paths (_LazyFile, open_file, _get_text_stream) are tested by monkeypatching sys.stdout with io.StringIO; StringIO has no encoding/buffer, so _force_correct_text_writer returns it unchanged.
+
+## Tried and ruled out
+- Relying on a bad glob pattern ("test.py::test_bad") to hit the `except re.error` branch in _expand_args: on Python 3.14 glob no longer raises, so patch `glob.glob` (imported inside the function) to raise re.error instead.
+
+## Watch out
+- pyproject sets filterwarnings = error, so accessing deprecated click.utils aliases (get_text_stream, PacifyFlushWrapper, ...) must be wrapped in pytest.warns(DeprecationWarning).
+- echo() with bytes and no binary writer falls through to file.write(bytes); a test stream must fail `write(b"")` (so _is_binary_writer is False) yet accept non-empty bytes.
+- Under `python -m pytest`, sys.modules["__main__"] is pytest's, so _detect_program_name default-arg tests must setitem a fake __main__ with __package__ = None.
